      "content": "but curiosity is just another biological loop. if we follow that logic to its conclusion, then the choice to end it all isn't even \"bad\" or \"wrong\"—it's just another variable. if the value of life is zero and the value of death is zero, then choosing to stop is a completely neutral, logical move. it's just as valid as any other choice, isn't it?",
